So this is my first review. I thought I would do it on a game I have played for a while.
I see a lot of reviews here from people with 30 hours. Those reviews should be moot. You can't experience the game in 30 hours.
That being said, this is an MMO. It is a very casual MMO. I played FFxi for years and years. I tried WoW, Rift, Lineage 2, Etc etc. FFxi was always my favorite MMO because of how epic the grind was and how hardcore the players were. FFxiv is not like that. FFxiv is as casual as you can get. They decided to go the route of WoW and the other recent MMO and just make a quest grind game. You start out quest grinding, and you end quest grinding.
The game is very beautiful. The graphics are top notch. It is the best looking MMO available currently. I don't see the graphics of this game being topped any time soon. There are very few bugs and the developers are quite in-tune to their player base. They usually have maintenance for about 3 hours, twice a week. The developers listen to feedback and input. The GM system is handled pretty quickly as well.
When it comes to the content, the bulk, the meaty center that holds the game together... there isn't much. Your choices of activity are limited. You can level a job, do a craft(
), run dungeons. The game has been out a little over a year, and with an expansion on the way, I hope this will change soon. Once you finish leveling your preferred job(
), or even all of the jobs. You are left with nothing but repeating content for equipment. Doing weekly quests to cap your "currency" so that you can afford a piece of gear that will be outdated in a couple months. It is a cycle, and has been since I started. You repeat content, get the points, buy the gear, then they make that gear obsolete and you do the exact same thing next update. That is all there is to this game. If you want a hardcore endgame experience, you won't find it with FFxiv.
My biggest letdown with FFxiv was the community. There is a lack of community. I don't mean a lack of players, because there are plenty. There is a lack of community. In FFxi and similar tight-knit end-game MMOs there were community. You
who the best players were at end-game, you saw them in town, you knew what the best guild(
) was. There were achievements that held the best above the rest. People were accountable for their actions and their attitudes. If someone was a♥♥♥♥♥♥and screwed people over by stealing your money, or constantly bailing on your group. They were shunned by the community and held accountable. This is not true for FFxiv. In this game, when you join a group for a dungeon, or any content really, you are grouped with random people from different servers. Who can screw with you just for fun, and they do. The "best" players are the people who did their weekly caps and got their gear. We used to call it "cookie cutter", now I am not sure what to call it. Everyone has the same equipment. Everyone has accomplished the same thing. Everyone is the same.

